From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:38:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 623/623] V1 Sampler: Fuse temperature scaling into Gumbel-max
 sampling kernel

When active requests only scale by temperature (no logit bias, penalties, bad
words, thinking budget, min_p, top_k, or top_p) and processed logprobs are not
requested:
- Skip allocating the [num_rows, vocab_size] FP32 copy and launching
  apply_temperature in Sampler.apply_sampling_params.
- Fuse temperature scaling into tilelang_sampling.gumbel_sample_kernel
  (apply_temperature=True) for target sampling.
- Add an in-kernel apply_temperature runtime flag to tilelang_rejection's
  local_stats_kernel, verify_kernel, and resample_kernel so block verification
  reads raw BF16 target logits directly.
